; Leg CS -- server mode on real hardware.  HW_TESTING leg 0.7, untouched
; since it was written.
;
; The Victor runs CKERMITW -x and waits.  Everything below is driven from
; this end.  Server mode has run under MAME (SS16i, milestone step 6) and
; never on the machine.
;
; WHY IT NEEDED A DECISION RATHER THAN A FIX, which is worth knowing before
; reading a failure here.  C-Kermit 11 initialises every en_* capability to
; "remote mode only", and a Victor that owns its serial line is by
; definition LOCAL, so a -x server ACKs the negotiation and then refuses
; every command with a well-formed E packet.  NOICP removes the prompt where
; you would type ENABLE GET.  ckvictor.c therefore settles the capability
; set from a priority-0 XI initializer.  So an E packet in reply to a
; well-formed command is the signature of that initializer not running, and
; is a different failure from the transfer itself going wrong.
;
; NOT INCLUDED, deliberately: REMOTE DIRECTORY streams its listing and never
; terminates it (SS16i, and it is still open).  Do not add it to this leg --
; it will hang and take the leg with it.
;
; BYE is also not sent.  It has never been sent in this port's life, and a
; leg that ends by shutting the far end down cannot be retried without a
; power cycle.  FINISH leaves the Victor at the DOS prompt with its exit
; report written, which is the whole point of running it.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aiCS.pkt
echo === CS 1: SEND to the server (host -> Victor)
send rcvcs.dat
statistics
echo === CS 2: GET from the server (Victor -> host)
get RCVCS.DAT gotcs.dat
statistics
echo === CS 3: FINISH -- the server exits, DOS prompt returns
finish
